spawnOverride: spawnSequence([fakeChild({ stdout: cliEnvelope({ recommendations: [{ skillId: 'sk-doc', score: 0.9, confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12, command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }] }) })]) })`, awaits `runPrompt(hooks)`, restores the variable in a `finally` and asserts that `output.system[0]` contains `sk-doc → /create:agent (start)`. This case passes today and fails when the plugin drops a field. Verify: `VP` reports `fail 0` and `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node TSX $PL/probe-plugin-fields.mts` prints `plugin test asserts a command label: true`.\n116: - [ ] T028 [P] Test the command fields on the fallback path (`ENV`). Add `it('keeps the command, its policy and its owner from a CLI row')`, which calls `resultFromCliData` with `data: { freshness: 'live', recommendations: [{ skillId: 'sk-doc', confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12, command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }] }` and the `options`, `startedAt` and `now` the existing cases pass, expects `result.recommendations[0]` to match `{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }` and expects the first line of `renderAdvisorBrief(result)` to contain `sk-doc → /create:agent (start)`. This case passes today and fails when a field is dropped. Verify: `VX tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n117: \n118: ### Wave 1, lane WG7: subprocess busy scan and catalog anchors\n119: - [ ] T029 [P] See a busy marker past the stderr cap (`SUB`, `SUBT`). Test first: in `SUBT`, rename the case `stops reading stderr at the cap, so a busy marker past it is not seen` to `retries once on a busy marker written after the cap`, expect `errorCode` `SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED` and `retriesAttempted` 1, and replace the comment above it with one saying the cap bounds what is kept, not what is scanned. Add